Apple's press release for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/apple-announces-foldable-iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> last week said the device <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-duo-ios-27-1/">will ship with iOS 27.1</a>, which essentially confirms the software update's release timing.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27-1-Beta-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1064871" /><br/>
iPhone Duo launches on Friday, October 23, so we can expect iOS 27.1 to be released by that date at the latest — likely several days earlier.<br/>
<br/>
Following three months of beta testing, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/14/ios-27-features-available-tomorrow/">iOS 27 will be released to the public today</a>, and the first beta of iOS 27.1 will likely follow soon after.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>New Features to Expect</h2><br/>
During its iPhone event last week, Apple announced that Siri AI will be available in French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish starting in October, and this expanded language support beyond English will likely arrive with iOS 27.1 based on that timeframe, as the software update itself will likely be released in October.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Siri-AI-More-Languages-October.jpg" alt="" width="2062" height="1162" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1064862" /><br/>
Apple recently said that <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/11/ios-27-delayed-features/">two new features will not be available in the initial iOS 27 release</a>, including suggestions like "Add to Reminders" and "Add to Notes" in the Messages app and the ability to automatically fix compromised passwords with a single tap in the Passwords app. Apple merely said these features will arrive in a "future software update," and iOS 27.1 will likely be the earliest opportunity for that to happen.<br/>
<br/>
And of course, iOS 27.1 supports the iPhone Duo's unique foldable interface.<br/>
<br/>
